# --- ML model artifacts ---
# Reversal from earlier in the project: these ARE committed now
# (ml-service/*/models/*.joblib, *.keras, *_classes.json — ~16MB total).
# A deployed ml-service needs working models on first boot, and two of the
# three (price_prediction, condition_assessment) can't be retrained on a
# fresh deploy anyway since their raw datasets aren't committed (see below) —
# an untrained fresh clone would 503 forever with no way to fix it short of
# manually re-uploading datasets. The models themselves are just weights, not
# a redistribution of the source data, so this doesn't reopen the dataset
# license concern below.

# --- Third-party datasets (Kaggle etc.) — redistribution license unclear,
# don't push someone else's dataset to a public repo. Keep the *.gitkeep
# and the small prepare_data.py-generated summaries (labels.csv, tag_map.json),
# not raw source files or copied images/CSVs. See ml-service/README section
# on regenerating training data locally. ---
ml-service/price_prediction/data/*.csv
ml-service/condition_assessment/data/Annotated Dataset of Car Parts with Damage/
ml-service/condition_assessment/data/Coco Car Damage Detection Dataset/
ml-service/condition_assessment/data/images/*.jpg
!ml-service/condition_assessment/data/images/.gitkeep

# --- Uploaded media (created at runtime by server/src/middleware/upload.js) ---
server/uploads/

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

